{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Types of Software Testing: part 2"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear or use to talk about software testing."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Implement and document the software tests, appling trial and error, based on the designed plan and procedures established by the company.  Applies the different types of software testing to the IT solution."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Discusses a range of options for potential actions at work through the correct use of grammar, vocabulary; level of formality and purpose, and cohesion and coherence aspects appropriate to this level.\tExchanges simple information on software testing, test estimation, and data migration processes "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": ""}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "end-user"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "person who ultimately uses a product"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Beta is performed by end-users before the software is released to the market."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "meet a requirement"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to fulfill or achieve a demanded goal"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The acceptance test requires the user or customers to test the system to see if it meets the requirements."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "feedback"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "opinion given after evaluating something or someone's performance  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The Beta allows users to use the product and they provide feedback."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "crystal clear"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "what someone says when there are no doubts about a topic and the person totally understood something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: It's crystal clear!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "go beyond"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to surpass or exceed a limit"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(phrasal verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Programmers may create special conditions to go beyond the system's capacities. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "measure"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to quantify something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think the compatibility test is used to measure the system's performance when it's used with certain hardware, software, operative system, network, and different combinations of all."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n6le03ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Conditional Sentences with If Clauses- Question Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Conditional clauses</span> are used to talk about a situation that becomes real or likely to happen only when a condition is fulfilled."}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I want to push the limits of software, what testing will I have to use?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If I want to push the limits of software, what testing will I have to use?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The usual conditional sentence is composed of 2 clauses: the <span class=\"strong\">if clause</span> that explains the condition, and the other clause that presents the result or consequence. <br/>  There are different types of conditional sentences with different degrees of grammatical structures. The <span class=\"strong\">first conditional</span> states something that might easily happen in the future. <br/>  Any of the two clauses can be affirmative, negative or even mixed in questions with conditional sentences. The <span class=\"strong\">first conditional</span> uses the simple future in the <span class=\"strong\">result clause</span> and simple present in the <span class=\"strong\">if clause</span>.<br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\">What computer <span class=\"strong\">will</span> you buy <span class=\"strong\">if</span> you need it to be good for programming? </span><br/><br/>  It's possible to put the <span class=\"strong\">if clause</span> at the beginning of the question. In that case, a <span class=\"strong\">comma</span> must be added. </span><br/><br/>  Example: <br/> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">If</span> you need a good computer for programing, what computer <span class=\"strong\">will</span> you buy? </span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Beta and Acceptance Testing"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Beta and Acceptance Testing</span> are fundamental because they engage users in the evaluation of software systems."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are different types of software testing that involve different people in different parts of the whole process. In this opportunity, the Beta and Acceptance testing involve users in the fundamental part of a software system approval. <br/><br/>  The <span class=\"strong\">Beta version</span> of a software system is a trial for checking the system's performance with real users or end-users, who are the ones the product is addressed to, and pinpoint possible mistakes or whatever needs to be corrected or improved in the program. <br/><br/>  The <span class=\"strong\">Acceptance Testing</span> occurs when all flaws have been corrected and users, who can be an enterprise's employees, interact with the final version of the system. They focus on whether the software accomplishes the goal or not. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Make a small presentation about other types of software testing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Specify in which case is appropriate to use each one"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the information with your classmates "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I read information about software testing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I understand the characteristics and appropriate use of each one"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about software testing "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "type": "welcome", "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"video_src": "enpe8n6le03ob03re2vid01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "", "id": 0, "text": "<p align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\">Carl</span>: Hi Edna. Would you help me with my assignment?<br />"}, {"time": "4000", "image": "", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Edna</span>: Sure! Is it about software testing? I know you've been taking some classes to improve your knowledge on computers. <br />"}, {"time": "11000", "image": "", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Carl</span>: Indeed. I just need a little help with some testing types I forgot to research about. The first two are closely related, I think, the Beta and Acceptance testing. <br />"}, {"time": "21200", "image": "", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Edna</span>: Ok. The Beta is performed by end-users before the software is released to the market. The acceptance test requires the user or customers to test the system to see if it meets the requirements. <br />"}, {"time": "34300", "image": "", "id": 4, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Carl</span>: If you can explain to me the difference, it will help me a lot. I don't understand what the difference is. <br />"}, {"time": "40800", "image": "", "id": 5, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Edna</span>: The Beta allows users to use the product and they provide feedback. The acceptance is the final testing performed by users. Got it?<br />"}, {"time": "50000", "image": "", "id": 6, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Carl</span>: It's crystal clear! If I want to push the limits of software, what testing will I have to use?<br />"}, {"time": "56000", "image": "", "id": 7, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Edna</span>: Stress testing definitely. You have to test the product under difficult and demanding conditions. It stretches the system's limits. Programmers may create special conditions to go beyond the system's capacities. <br />"}, {"time": "70500", "image": "", "id": 8, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Carl</span>: Thanks, Edna. Just the last one. If you want to test the positive and negative features of software, will you choose comparison test?<br />"}, {"time": "78500", "image": "", "id": 9, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Edna</span>: Yes, it's suitable. The comparison testing compares the strengths and weaknesses of a system with previous versions of the system or similar ones. People may confuse the comparison with the compatibility test. <br />"}, {"time": "93300", "image": "", "id": 10, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Carl</span>: I think the compatibility test is used to measure the system's performance when it's used with certain hardware, software, operative system, network, and different combinations of all. <br />"}, {"time": "104300", "image": "", "id": 11, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Edna</span>: You have that one clear! I think you don't need my help anymore.<br /></p>"}]}, "type": "video"}], "type": "video", "_data": [], "id": 3, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about beta testing and acceptance testing. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe stress testing characteristics."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain comparison and compatibility testing."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What kind of software do you consider needs more testing before being released? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "How do you imagine testing occurs in videogames? "}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "try again"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time"}], "allowed_attempts": 2}}, {"type": "free_header_text", "content": "Ask your partner: "}, {"type": "free_type_text_area", "content": "Software Testing Types and Purposes"}], "img_path": "", "id": 0}, {"stimuli_ids": [3], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"correct": 0, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "selected": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1}], "id": 0}], "type": "STI", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "tex